<%# Name, feed, state, count, and the two ways to stop hearing from a blog.

    Muting and removing are both POSTs, so both are buttons rather than links
    — see .claude/rules/views.md. Only removing confirms, because only
    removing is irreversible: the posts go, and so do the citations in
    published editions naming them. Muting takes nothing and can be undone
    from this same row, so a confirmation would be ceremony over a decision
    the reader can see the result of immediately.

    Each button carries its own accessible name. Every row's says "Remove"
    and "Mute", so a reader who cannot see which row they are in has nothing
    to tell three of them apart. %>
<li class="pen__item pen__item--source">
  <span class="sources__name"><%= row.name %></span>
  <% if row.feed? %>
    <span class="sources__feed"><%= row.feed_url %></span>
  <% end %>
  <span class="<%= row.state_class %>"><%= row.state %></span>
  <span class="sources__count"><%= row.count %></span>
  <% if row.silenced? %>
    <span class="sources__state sources__state--muted"><%= row.muted %></span>
    <%= button_to t(".unmute"), blog_silence_path(row), method: :delete,
          class: "sources__mute", form_class: "sources__mute-form",
          aria: { label: t(".unmute_blog", name: row.name) } %>
  <% else %>
    <%= button_to t(".mute"), blog_silence_path(row),
          class: "sources__mute", form_class: "sources__mute-form",
          aria: { label: t(".mute_blog", name: row.name) } %>
  <% end %>
  <%= button_to t(".remove"), blog_path(row), method: :delete,
        class: "sources__remove", form_class: "sources__remove-form",
        aria: { label: t(".remove_blog", name: row.name) },
        data: { turbo_confirm: t(".confirm", name: row.name) } %>
</li>
